{"id": "fixed-dilated-pupil", "site": "eye", "definition": {"all": [{"obs": "eye.pupil", "path": "reaction", "op": "eq", "value": "absent"}, {"obs": "eye.pupil", "path": "sizeMm", "op": "ge", "value": 5.5, "ctx": {"lightOn": "none", "ambient": "room"}}]}, "threshold": {"text": "no constriction to light in a pupil of 5.5 mm or more in room light; a third-nerve pupil is typically 6–7 mm. A blind eye’s pupil does not react to its own light either, but it is not dilated and it constricts with the other eye’s light: that is an afferent defect, not this sign", "status": "assumed"}, "status": "draft"},
